        "question_BMXtrX": {
          "type": "question",
          "settings": {
            "question": "What are ball back studs?",
            "answer": "<p>Ball back studs are a style of piercing jewellery featuring a rounded ball end instead of a flat disc. The smooth ball sits comfortably at the back of the piercing, making them ideal for ear, cartilage, and lip piercings.</p>",
            "icon": "none"
          }
        },
        "question_tbki47": {
          "type": "question",
          "settings": {
            "question": "Are silver and steel ball back studs safe for sensitive skin?",
            "answer": "<p>Yes. Our <strong>surgical steel</strong> ball back studs are<br/>hypoallergenic and safe for most skin types. <strong>Sterling silver</strong> is suitable for healed piercings but may not be ideal for very fresh piercings, as silver can oxidise. If your piercing is new, it’s best to start with titanium or steel before switching to silver once healed.</p>",
            "icon": "none"
          }
        },
        "question_DWBnyC": {
          "type": "question",
          "settings": {
            "question": "What piercings can ball back studs be used for?",
            "answer": "<p>Ball back studs are versatile and can be worn in a range of piercings including <strong>helix</strong>, <strong>lobe</strong>, <strong>conch</strong>, <strong>tragus</strong>, <strong>lip</strong>, and <strong>cartilage piercings</strong>. The rounded back makes them particularly comfortable for areas that may experience friction.</p>",
            "icon": "none"
          }
        },
        "question_4KcKKD": {
          "type": "question",
          "settings": {
            "question": "Are your ball back studs externally or internally threaded?",
            "answer": "<p>Most of our ball back studs are <strong>externally threaded</strong> for a secure and classic fit. Each piece is precision-made to ensure a smooth thread that won’t irritate the piercing.</p>",
            "icon": "none"
          }
